{title: Lighthouse Keeper}
{artist: Arlo Fenn}

{start_of_verse: Verse}
[Em]He counts th[C]e ships he’ll never board
[G]Paints the rail [D]and oils the door
[Em]“Stay a while,” [C]the sea says, “stay”
[G]And he does it [D]every day
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[C]Turn the [G]light, turn the light
[D]Somebody’s [Em]out there tonight
[C]Turn the [G]light, turn the light
[D]Bring them ho[Em]me alright
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse}
[Em]Winter takes [C]the gulls away
[G]Leaves him logbo[D]oks, leaves him grey
[Em]Still he climbs [C]the hundred stairs
[G]No one knows and [D]no one cares
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[C]Turn the [G]light, turn the light
[D]Somebody’s [Em]out there tonight
[C]Turn the [G]light, turn the light
[D]Bring them ho[Em]me alright
{end_of_chorus}
